{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-p-bandwidth-bound","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:p-bandwidth-bound","kind":"proposition","title":"Polynomial computation as sub-horizon bandwidth","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-computational-horizon"],"tags":["P-class","bandwidth","information-flow","planck-step","complexity","polynomial-time"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.p_bandwidth_bound","text":"p-bandwidth-bound.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:p-bandwidth-bound\"></a><p>A decision problem encoded by a link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L = \\hat{\\beta}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c = 3N</code> crossings belongs to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{P}</code> if and only if its Skein polynomial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_L(q)</code> can be evaluated (its degree-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> answer extracted) within</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  t(c) \\leq \\mathfrak{B}(q)^{-1} \\mathrm{poly}(c)</code></pre>\n<p>Planck steps, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{B}(q) = q\\eta_q / (q-1)^2</code> is the information bandwidth per Planck time.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/p-bandwidth-bound.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"22.7.3","page":"b/prop-p-bandwidth-bound","qa":{"counts":{"pass":92,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":84},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.InformationTheory.p_bandwidth_bound","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/InformationTheory/p_bandwidth_bound.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryB